---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const orgLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Organization',
  name: 'The Melanotan Record',
  url: Astro.site?.href,
  description:
    'An independent publication covering the history and analysis of Melanotan II and the melanocortin drug class.',
  publishingPrinciples: new URL('/standards/', Astro.site).href,
  correctionsPolicy: new URL('/standards/', Astro.site).href,
  knowsAbout: [
    'Melanotan II',
    'Melanotan I',
    'afamelanotide',
    'bremelanotide',
    'melanocortin receptors',
    'alpha-melanocyte-stimulating hormone',
  ],
};
---
<Base
  title="Editorial standards — The Melanotan Record"
  description="How The Melanotan Record reports: primary sources, dated claims, plainly stated harms — and the lines it will never cross. The standard this site is written to."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(orgLd)} is:inline />
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Editorial standards</p>
    <h1>The standard this site is written to</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The Melanotan Record is an independent publication. Every article here is
      written to one editorial standard, and this page is that standard, set
      down in the open so any reader &mdash; or any regulator, dermatologist, or
      skeptical journalist &mdash; can hold the work to it.
    </p>

    <h2>Who writes this</h2>
    <p>
      The Melanotan Record is written and edited under a single masthead rather
      than under individual bylines. The name on every article is the
      publication&rsquo;s, and the standard on this page is the author of
      record. We claim no medical or clinical credentials, and we never borrow
      them: nothing here is written in the voice of a doctor giving advice,
      because it is not.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are independent of the industry we cover. The Record is not affiliated
      with, funded by, or speaking for any manufacturer, vendor, clinic, or any
      of the companies whose drugs appear in these pages. It sells nothing.
    </p>

    <h2>How we report</h2>
    <p>
      Every article is built from primary sources &mdash; peer-reviewed
      literature, patent filings, regulatory records, and companies&rsquo; own
      disclosures &mdash; and the specific claims are checked against those
      sources before anything is published. Dates, names, and numbers are meant
      to be verifiable; where a patent, trial, or approval is cited, it is a
      real one you can look up.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every article is dated. Where the evidence is thin, the article says so.
      Where a popular claim is wrong, the article says that too &mdash; including
      claims made by people selling things. For the receptor-level science
      underneath the history, we point to our sister reference,
      <a href="https://melanocortin.com" rel="noopener">melanocortin.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What we never publish</h2>
    <p>
      No sourcing, suppliers, dosing, or usage guidance for unapproved
      compounds &mdash; not framed as harm reduction, not framed as history.
      No commerce on this domain. No medical advice. Melanotan II is not
      approved by any regulator for any use, and this site treats it as the
      cautionary tale it is, not a manual for it.
    </p>

    <h2>Where we&rsquo;re opinionated, and say so</h2>
    <p>
      The Record holds one openly stated position: that the world still needs
      what the original researchers were chasing &mdash; a rigorously tested,
      approved medicine that gives skin durable protection from ultraviolet
      damage. When we argue that case, we label it as what it is: hope, clearly
      marked, kept separate from the reporting. The reasoning behind it lives on
      the <a href="/about/">about page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      When we find an error, or one is brought to our attention, we fix it and
      note the date of any material change. Freshness is only signalled when the
      substance of an article actually changed &mdash; we do not restamp dates to
      look current. An accurate record is worth more than a fresh-looking one.
    </p>
  </article>
  <style>
    article { padding-top: 2.5rem; }
    h1 { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.4rem); margin: 0.35rem 0 0.75rem; }
    .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 2rem; }
    .prose h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; }
  </style>
</Base>
